  <title>
    <media type="image" width="40px" height="40px" its:translate="no" src="figures/orca-logo.svg" /> Preferences
  </title>
  <p>
    Orca's global Preferences window includes all settings, including those for web content,
    chat, and spell checking. In earlier versions of Orca, settings for these features were
    available only in application preferences, so using the same non-default configuration in
    several browsers or chat applications required configuring each one separately. You can now
    configure them once in global preferences. Settings that do not apply to an application are
    simply not used.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can configure Orca differently for individual applications. Application preferences
    override global preferences for that application in the selected profile. Settings without
    an application-specific override continue to use the global configuration.
  </p>
  <p>
    To use a different value in an application, open its application preferences, change the
    setting, and save. Repeat for other applications as needed. To make an application follow
    the global setting again, set the application value to the global value and save. Orca
    removes the matching override, so later changes to the global setting also apply to that
    application.
  </p>
  <section id="opening-preferences">
    <title>Opening preferences</title>
    <p>
      Use the commands below to open the global or application Preferences window.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can also run <code>orca -s</code> or <code>orca --setup</code> in a terminal or your
      desktop's Run dialog to start Orca and open the global Preferences window. If Orca is
      already running, this opens its global Preferences window instead.
    </p>
    <section id="commands-opening-preferences">
      <title>Commands</title>
      <p>
        <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
        <gui>Commands</gui> category, <gui>Commands</gui> section, <gui>Screen Reader Management</gui> group.
      </p>
      <list>
        <item>
          <p>
            <gui>Display the preferences window</gui>: <keyseq>
              <key>Orca Modifier</key>
              <key>Space</key>
            </keyseq>
          </p>
        </item>
        <item>
          <p>
            <gui>Display the application preferences window</gui>: <keyseq>
              <key>Orca Modifier</key>
              <key>Ctrl</key>
              <key>Space</key>
            </keyseq>
          </p>
        </item>
      </list>
    </section>
  </section>
  <section id="changing-and-saving-settings">
    <title>Changing and saving settings</title>
    <p>
      Settings are grouped into categories in the side panel on the left. Use <key>Up Arrow</key> and <key>Down Arrow</key> to choose a category. As you
      change categories, the panel on the right displays that category's settings. Press <key>Tab</key> to move into that panel.
    </p>
    <p>
      Some categories contain subcategories. Use <key>Up Arrow</key> and <key>Down Arrow</key> to choose one, then <key>Right Arrow</key> or <key>Enter</key> to open it. Press <key>Left Arrow</key> or <key>Escape</key> to return to the subcategory list.
      From the main settings list, press <key>Left Arrow</key> to return to the sidebar. Use <key>Tab</key> and <keyseq>
        <key>Shift</key>
        <key>Tab</key>
      </keyseq>
      to move among controls.
    </p>
    <p>
      The "Options" menu button is at the top of the left panel. Press <key>F10</key> to move to "Options". You can also
      reach it from the sidebar with <keyseq>
        <key>Shift</key>
        <key>Tab</key>
      </keyseq>. Press <key>Enter</key> or <key>Space</key> to open the menu. Use the "Options"
      menu's apply action to save your changes without closing the window, or its save action to
      save and close it.
    </p>
    <p>
      The "Options" menu's "Cancel" action closes the window and discards unsaved preference
      edits. Changes already applied remain saved.
    </p>
    <p>
      Preferences is a window, not a dialog: <key>Escape</key> does not close it. Close it with <keyseq>
        <key>Alt</key>
        <key>F4</key>
      </keyseq>
      or the "Options" menu. If you press <keyseq>
        <key>Alt</key>
        <key>F4</key>
      </keyseq>
      with unsaved changes, Orca prompts you to save them, close without saving, or cancel and
      return to preferences. In global preferences, you can also save the changes as a new
      profile.
    </p>
